TOC levels are identified mainly by section number depth:

- Equipment headers (unnumbered all-caps or HEADER pattern): level -1 (equipment_block) — root anchor, sits above all numbered sections
- L0: whole number only, like 1, 2, 3 — numbered top-level within an equipment block
- L1: one dot, like 1.1, 2.1, 3.1
- L2: two dots, like 3.1.1
- L3: three dots, like 3.1.1.1 (if present)

Equipment block (level -1) only closes when the next equipment header is detected.
Numbered L0 headings (1, 2, 3) never close an equipment block span.

Parent-context rule (explicit):
- Once an equipment header is detected (for example STEAM TURBINE (370T031 | SY1392002)), all following local headings in that block (1, 1.1, 1.2, 2, 2.1, 3, 3.1) stay under that equipment parent block until the next equipment header appears.
- Their local level (L0/L1/L2/L3) is still determined by numbering depth, but equipment context does not reset just because numbering increments.



